($s$dev.backend-core.rest-api-design-reliability.q1$s$, $s$rest-api-design$s$, $s$lesson-rest-api-design$s$, $s$mcq$s$, $s$easy$s$, ARRAY[]::text[], $s${"id":"dev.backend-core.rest-api-design-reliability.q1","skill_id":"rest-api-design","lesson_id":"lesson-rest-api-design","prompt":"A client times out on POST /payments and retries with the same Idempotency-Key. What should the server do?","explanation":"The key identifies the operation; the server replays the saved response so a retry never repeats the side effect.","difficulty":"easy","company_tags":[],"status":"draft","ai_drafted":true,"version":1,"kind":"mcq","options":["Create a second payment","Return 409 always","Return the stored result of the first request without charging again","Ignore the key"],"correct":[2]}$s$::jsonb, $s$draft$s$, TRUE, 1),
