($s$dev.databases.postgresql-internals.q2$s$, $s$postgresql$s$, $s$lesson-postgresql$s$, $s$mcq$s$, $s$easy$s$, ARRAY[]::text[], $s${"id":"dev.databases.postgresql-internals.q2","skill_id":"postgresql","lesson_id":"lesson-postgresql","prompt":"Why do apps use a connection pool with PostgreSQL?","explanation":"Every PostgreSQL connection is a separate process with memory overhead, so reusing pooled connections scales better.","difficulty":"easy","company_tags":[],"status":"draft","ai_drafted":true,"version":1,"kind":"mcq","options":["Pools make SQL queries shorter","PostgreSQL forbids more than one connection","Pools replace the need for indexes","Each connection is costly, so reusing a few connections handles many requests efficiently"],"correct":[3]}$s$::jsonb, $s$draft$s$, TRUE, 1),
