($s$dev.backend-scale.caching.q1$s$, $s$caching$s$, $s$lesson-caching$s$, $s$mcq$s$, $s$easy$s$, ARRAY[]::text[], $s${"id":"dev.backend-scale.caching.q1","skill_id":"caching","lesson_id":"lesson-caching","prompt":"In the cache-aside pattern, what does the application do on a cache miss?","explanation":"In cache-aside the application owns loading: it reads the database on a miss and populates the cache itself.","difficulty":"easy","company_tags":[],"status":"draft","ai_drafted":true,"version":1,"kind":"mcq","options":["Returns an error so the client retries later","Reads from the database, returns the value and stores it in the cache with a TTL","Waits for the cache to load the value from the database by itself","Writes an empty value to the cache and returns nothing"],"correct":[1]}$s$::jsonb, $s$draft$s$, TRUE, 1),
