($s$dev.backend-scale.message-queues-patterns.q1$s$, $s$message-queues$s$, $s$lesson-message-queues$s$, $s$mcq$s$, $s$easy$s$, ARRAY[]::text[], $s${"id":"dev.backend-scale.message-queues-patterns.q1","skill_id":"message-queues","lesson_id":"lesson-message-queues","prompt":"An order service saves an order and then publishes OrderPlaced, but sometimes crashes in between. What fixes this?","explanation":"The outbox makes the event part of the same DB transaction; a relay publishes it later, so neither side is lost.","difficulty":"easy","company_tags":[],"status":"draft","ai_drafted":true,"version":1,"kind":"mcq","options":["Publishing the event before saving the order","Increasing the broker retention period","A transactional outbox written in the same DB transaction","Using a fanout exchange"],"correct":[2]}$s$::jsonb, $s$draft$s$, TRUE, 1),
