($s$dev.backend-scale.microservices.q1$s$, $s$microservices$s$, $s$lesson-microservices$s$, $s$mcq$s$, $s$easy$s$, ARRAY[]::text[], $s${"id":"dev.backend-scale.microservices.q1","skill_id":"microservices","lesson_id":"lesson-microservices","prompt":"The orders service needs a customer email that lives in the users service. What is the recommended approach?","explanation":"Services own their data; others use the owner's API or subscribe to its events instead of reading its tables.","difficulty":"easy","company_tags":[],"status":"draft","ai_drafted":true,"version":1,"kind":"mcq","options":["Query the users table directly from the orders service","Call the users service API, or keep a local copy updated from user events","Merge the two databases into one shared schema","Store the email in a shared config file"],"correct":[1]}$s$::jsonb, $s$draft$s$, TRUE, 1),
